IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `whs-worker`

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 -- worked cases, from the seat of the worker.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2024C00243), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Act;
-- every case is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Priya (HYPOTHETICAL) is an APS employee in a Commonwealth department's warehouse. On 2 March 2026 a forklift's mast
-- is leaking hydraulic fluid and its load is swaying above the aisle where she is told to pick stock.

§ `cases`

§§ `ss 7, 12, 12A`

#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` `the Commonwealth, such as a department or agency, or the Defence Force` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: this Act applies to my work for the Commonwealth or a public authority (s 12(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` `a Commonwealth public authority or Commonwealth company` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: this Act applies to my work for the Commonwealth or a public authority (s 12(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` `a non-Commonwealth licensee (a company licensed under the Comcare scheme)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: this Act applies to my work for a non-Commonwealth licensee in its transitional period (s 12(4))`
-- A licensee whose transitional period has ended, and a private employer: the State or Territory law (not covered).
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` `a non-Commonwealth licensee (a company licensed under the Comcare scheme)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `work for a business or undertaking that is not the Commonwealth's, a public authority's or a non-Commonwealth licensee's is under the State or Territory WHS law, which is not encoded (s 12)`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` `the ACT or NT administration, a State or local government, or a private business` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `work for a business or undertaking that is not the Commonwealth's, a public authority's or a non-Commonwealth licensee's is under the State or Territory WHS law, which is not encoded (s 12)`
-- On a ship under the Maritime Industry OHS Act, even for the Commonwealth: this Act does not apply (s 12A).
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` `the Commonwealth, such as a department or agency, or the Defence Force` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `answered` `no: this Act does not apply on a vessel or structure under the Occupational Health and Safety (Maritime Industry) Act 1993, or an offshore petroleum facility (s 12A)`

-- Priya, an employee: a worker. A volunteer at a volunteer association with no employees is not (s 5(7)).
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a worker` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a worker` FALSE FALSE

§§ `s 19`

#ASSERT `What must my employer ensure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `my health and safety while at work, so far as is reasonably practicable, by eliminating risks or, if that is not reasonably practicable, minimising them (ss 17, 19(1))`, `a work environment without risks to health and safety (s 19(3)(a))`, `safe plant and structures (s 19(3)(b))`, `safe systems of work (s 19(3)(c))`, `the safe use, handling and storage of plant, structures and substances (s 19(3)(d))`, `adequate facilities for my welfare at work, and access to them (s 19(3)(e))`, `the information, training, instruction or supervision needed to protect me (s 19(3)(f))`, `monitoring of my health and of conditions at the workplace to prevent illness or injury (s 19(3)(g))`
-- A Defence Force member in remote base housing that is the only accommodation available: the s 19(4) duty too.
#ASSERT `What must my employer ensure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST `my health and safety while at work, so far as is reasonably practicable, by eliminating risks or, if that is not reasonably practicable, minimising them (ss 17, 19(1))`, `a work environment without risks to health and safety (s 19(3)(a))`, `safe plant and structures (s 19(3)(b))`, `safe systems of work (s 19(3)(c))`, `the safe use, handling and storage of plant, structures and substances (s 19(3)(d))`, `adequate facilities for my welfare at work, and access to them (s 19(3)(e))`, `the information, training, instruction or supervision needed to protect me (s 19(3)(f))`, `monitoring of my health and of conditions at the workplace to prevent illness or injury (s 19(3)(g))`, `the accommodation it provides me, maintained so that I am not exposed to risks (s 19(4))`
-- A business that neither engaged her nor directs her work owes her none of the s 19(1) duties.
#ASSERT `What must my employer ensure` FALSE FALSE EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `ss 47 to 49`

-- The department proposes a new picking system for the warehouse: Priya is directly affected and has an HSR.
#ASSERT `Must my employer consult me` `proposing changes that may affect workers' health or safety` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the business must consult me through my health and safety representative, who must be involved (ss 47, 48(2))`
#ASSERT `Must my employer consult me` `identifying hazards or assessing risks from the work` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the business must consult me, so far as is reasonably practicable, sharing the information, letting me give my views and contribute, taking them into account and telling me the outcome (ss 47, 48(1))`
#ASSERT `Must my employer consult me` `proposing changes that may affect workers' health or safety` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 49 does not list this matter, or I am not directly affected by it`
#ASSERT `Must my employer consult me` `something else` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 49 does not list this matter, or I am not directly affected by it`

§§ `ss 50, 80 to 82`

#ASSERT `May I ask for an HSR election` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I ask for an HSR election` FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I take the issue to an inspector` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: the parties must first make reasonable efforts to resolve it under the agreed or default procedure (ss 81(2), 82(1))`
#ASSERT `Can I take the issue to an inspector` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I may ask Comcare to appoint an inspector to help resolve it (s 82(2)); I keep my right to stop unsafe work (s 82(3))`
#ASSERT `Can I take the issue to an inspector` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `my health and safety representative, as the party for my work group, may ask Comcare to appoint an inspector (ss 80(1)(c), 82(2))`

§§ `ss 84 to 88`

-- Priya, under the swaying load: a reasonable concern of a serious risk from an imminent exposure. She may refuse.
#ASSERT `May I stop unsafe work` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may cease or refuse the work (s 84); I must tell the business as soon as practicable and stay available for suitable alternative work (s 86)`
-- A concern about long-term exposure to dust, not immediate or imminent: no s 84 right (the issue procedure is the way).
#ASSERT `May I stop unsafe work` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the right to stop work needs a reasonable concern of a serious risk to my health or safety from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard (s 84)`
#ASSERT `May I stop unsafe work` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the right to stop work needs a reasonable concern of a serious risk to my health or safety from an immediate or imminent exposure to a hazard (s 84)`
-- Her HSR directs the aisle cleared: she must stop, and need not notify the department herself.
#ASSERT `May I stop unsafe work` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I must cease on my health and safety representative's direction (s 85); I must stay available for suitable alternative work, and need not tell the business myself (s 86)`
-- She is sent to pack orders in the next building and does so: continuity protected. She refuses unreasonably: not.
#ASSERT `Is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my continuity of engagement protected` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my continuity of engagement protected` FALSE FALSE

§§ `ss 28, 31 to 34, Schedule 4`

#ASSERT `What are my duties as a worker` EQUALS LIST `take reasonable care for my own health and safety (s 28(a))`, `take reasonable care that my acts or omissions do not adversely affect the health and safety of others (s 28(b))`, `comply, so far as I am reasonably able, with any reasonable instruction the business gives to comply with the Act (s 28(c))`, `co-operate with any reasonable health or safety policy or procedure of the business that has been notified to workers (s 28(d))`
-- A worker (column 3 of Schedule 4 cl 1): category 1, $1,500,000 or 15 years or both; category 2, $209,000; category 3,
-- $70,000; industrial manslaughter cannot be committed by a worker as such (s 30A(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker` `category 1: negligent or reckless conduct, without reasonable excuse, exposing someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 31)` EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 1500000, 15)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker` `category 2: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty that exposes someone to a risk of death or serious injury or illness (s 32)` EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 209000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker` `category 3: a failure to comply with a health and safety duty (s 33)` EQUALS JUST (`Maximum penalty` OF 70000, 0)
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined as a worker` `industrial manslaughter: intentional conduct breaching a health and safety duty that causes a death, reckless or negligent as to it (s 30A)` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 35 to 37`

-- The load falls and Priya's foot is crushed; she is admitted to hospital: notifiable (s 36(a)).
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident` `someone needed immediate treatment as a hospital in-patient` FALSE TRUE
-- The load falls and hits nobody: still a dangerous incident, a fall from a height exposing her to a serious risk (s 37(f)).
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident` `someone was exposed to a serious risk from an immediate or imminent uncontrolled escape, spill, fire, explosion, gas or steam leak, electric shock, fall from height, collapse or failure listed in s 37` FALSE TRUE
-- A sprained wrist treated at the GP: not notifiable.
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a notifiable incident` `another injury, illness or incident` FALSE TRUE
-- A kind the regulations exclude, and a kind they add.
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a notifiable incident` `someone needed medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a notifiable incident` `another injury, illness or incident` TRUE TRUE
-- A death that did not arise out of the business's work (a visitor's heart attack): not notifiable by it.
#ASSERT NOT `Is it a notifiable incident` `someone died` FALSE FALSE

§§ `ss 104 to 106, 112, 113, 115`

-- Priya is moved to night shifts because she refused the aisle: detriment, for a prohibited reason (s 106(d)).
#ASSERT `Can I go to court over discrimination` `I was put to my detriment, or my position was altered to my detriment` `I stopped unsafe work, or exercised or proposed to exercise another power or function under the Act` FALSE EQUALS `yes: I may apply to a court for an injunction, compensation, reinstatement or another order (s 112); the safety reason is presumed a substantial reason unless they prove otherwise (s 113(2)), and they have a defence only if the conduct was reasonable and done substantially to comply with the Act (s 113(3))`
-- Dismissed for raising the forklift with the HSR, and a Fair Work general protections application already lodged and
-- not withdrawn: no s 112 proceeding (s 115(a)).
#ASSERT `Can I go to court over discrimination` `I was dismissed, or my contract for services was ended` `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern` TRUE EQUALS `no: I have another proceeding, application or complaint about the same matter under another Commonwealth or State law that is not withdrawn (s 115(a))`
#ASSERT `Can I go to court over discrimination` `I was dismissed, or my contract for services was ended` `another reason` FALSE EQUALS `no: it was not done for a reason s 106 prohibits`
#ASSERT `Can I go to court over discrimination` `nothing of these` `I raised, or proposed to raise, a health or safety issue or concern` FALSE EQUALS `no: what was done is not discriminatory conduct under s 105`
-- Told of the move on 16 March 2026: proceedings by 16 March 2027 (s 113(1)).
#ASSERT `By when must I go to court over discrimination` (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS Date 16 3 2027
